post.description:
One error from an application, with the project's key. Events with the same exception type and the same last three frames of your own code (or the same message, with numbers and quoted text ignored) are one issue. A resolved issue that happens again is reopened as a regression.

```bash
curl -sf -X POST https://errors.example.com/api/v1/events -H "x-errors-key: $ERRORS_KEY" -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{
  "release": "1.4.2", "environment": "production", "user": {"id": "u-42"},
  "exception": {"type": "TypeError", "value": "x is undefined", "frames": [{"filename": "src/cart.js", "function": "total", "lineno": 12, "in_app": true}]}
}'
```

The body may be gzipped (`Content-Encoding: gzip`), up to 1 MiB unpacked. A project may send a limited number of events a minute; over it, the answer is 429 with `Retry-After`, and the event is not stored.

Takes a project key.
